<title>SPAIN: Spanish police fend off cows at milk quota protest.</title>
<headline>Spanish police fend off cows at milk quota protest.</headline>
<text>
<p>MADRID, Oct 1 (Reuter) Spanish police wrestled farmers and threw up barricades to keep cows back at a rowdy protest in Madrid on Tuesday against European Union milk quotas.</p>
<p>Riot police with shields shoved back about 300 farmers pushing with a dozen cows towards the Agriculture Ministry after the demonstrators tossed pails of milk at them.</p>
<p>The farmers, from all over Spain, were protesting at EU milk quotas. They demanded that Spain's share be raised from 5.4 million tonnes a year to seven million.</p>
</text>
